# Firestore rules

```
// BAD
allow read, write: if true;
allow write: if request.auth != null; // any signed-in user writes anything

// GOOD
match /{document=**} { allow read, write: if false; }
match /public_contacts/{id} { allow read: if true; allow write: if false; }
match /users/{uid} {
  allow read: if request.auth.uid == uid;
  allow create, update: if request.auth.uid == uid
    && !request.resource.data.keys().hasAny(['role', 'isAdmin', 'isPremium']);
}
```

- `admins/{uid}` is Console/Admin SDK only. Apps never create their own admin doc.
- Public collections: only fields you would print on a store listing.
- Private collections: `allow read, write: if false` and write via Admin SDK or a callable.
- Storage: deny all until a week actually needs uploads; then path must include `uid`.
